eate three style frames and one  finished Motion test the star map  screens convey complex decoded data on  unknown star systems I had to consider  the mapping elements solar systems and  nebula's measurements and Direction  systems grid systems shapes depth and  blur typography and it had to have a  handheld motion for the tone mood and  style it had to have organic and  circular shapes Moody analog texture and  simple colors two to three tones based  on this creative brief I started  Gathering images for visual inspiration  let's look at my workflow when it comes  to designing mood boards I first went on  Pinterest and created The Screen  Graphics board where I pinned everything  that I found visually interesting this  took some time but I did set myself a  time constraints in the same way I  created this retro board with retro  elements I found to be visually  interesting from there I jumped into  pure rap and dried and dropped the  images from Pinterest that were most  inspiring to me the goal here wasn't to  get inspired by one piece in particular  but to take inspiration from let's say  this piece here with elements from this  board over there and mix it with maybe  some symbols you like on this board here  you can then try and make something that  is truly original and that no one has  seen before if you want to save all the  images you've imported into pure wrap  you can press Ctrl a to select them all  right click save export and save all  images to a designated folder when it  came to designing the wireframe I was  inspired by these two pictures and their  original sci-fi retro layouts for this  left part I was inspired by this grid  and all of the other similar grids with  sharp or rounded Corners I found on  these boards for the style frames you  could see how I gathered and used all  this inspiration to create these final  designs you can see the typography depth  in blur simple colors you can also see  the round circular shapes and UI  elements in the 